        answer: `Triad: asthma, chronic rhinosinusitis with nasal polyps (CRSwNP), and respiratory reactions to aspirin and other COX-1 inhibitors (NSAIDs).\nEponym: Samter’s triad.\nEurope: NSAID-exacerbated respiratory disease (N-ERD, NERD).\nNot IgE-mediated: the reaction is pharmacologic (COX-1 inhibition), so every COX-1 inhibitor cross-reacts.`,
