        brief: 'The only randomized trial in a pure AERD population: small, single-centre, atopic patients only. Ten of 16 tolerated aspirin on omalizumab, versus none on placebo.',
        detailed: `Hayashi 2020 (PubMed 32142372): double-blind, randomized, crossover, single-centre (Sagamihara); atopic AERD diagnosed by systemic aspirin challenge; washout over 18 weeks. Primary endpoint: area under the log urinary LTE4 vs time curve during oral challenge (median 51.1 vs 80.8, P<0.001). Omalizumab also reduced upper and lower airway symptoms during challenge. The 0% placebo figure is from Priessnitz Table 1.\n\nMethodological point: atopy was an entry criterion, so the result does not establish the same effect in non-atopic AERD. Crossover with 16 completers gives precision on a biomarker, not on clinical outcomes.\n\nApplication: the evidence base for using a biologic to bridge to ATAD (Case 2 and item q51).`,
