        brief: 'Positive but indirect: the RCT result is in CRSwNP overall ("irrespective of NSAID sensitivity"), and the AERD-specific data are a small retrospective series.',
        detailed: `SYNAPSE (Han 2021, PubMed 33872587): 407 patients with recurrent, refractory severe CRSwNP and prior surgery, 100 mg SC every 4 weeks for 52 weeks; NPS adjusted difference in medians −0.73 and nasal obstruction VAS −3.14 vs placebo. Priessnitz §3.3.2: about 27% (108/407) had AERD; 57% lower risk of sinus surgery; specific AERD subgroup results not separately published.\n\nTuttle 2018 (n=14, retrospective): SNOT-22 −17.7 after 3 to 6 months, less congestion and anosmia, no sinus surgery; ACT +5.1; FEV1 trended up 5 to 6% predicted; with longer use, exacerbations fell and five patients reduced maintenance OCS (Priessnitz §3.3.2–3.3.3).\n\nPearl: Priessnitz notes patient outcomes on anti-IL-5 were "subpar" relative to the eosinophil rationale (§3.3.1).`,
